{"id": "EUVD-2026-104291", "enisaUuid": "b55784ef-5d37-30dc-bab4-dc998845f7dd", "description": "VideoLAN libbluray through 1.5.1 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in clpi_access_point() that allows attackers to crash applications by supplying a ClipInfo file with an empty EP-map fine table. Attackers can place a crafted .clpi file in BDMV/CLIPINF with num_ep_fine set to zero and an unclamped ref_ep_fine_id, triggering reads during seeking for denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:42:52", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libbluray-clpi-ep-map-oob-read", "https://code.videolan.org/videolan/libbluray/-/blob/1.5.1/src/libbluray/bdnav/clpi_parse.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/videolan-libbluray-through-1.5.1-out-of-bounds-read-via-clpi-access-point"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x3j6-3979-c9q8", "CVE-2026-112282"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "780f8e53-1362-3233-8e26-9bbf8931f0a3", "product": {"name": "libbluray", "vendor": {"name": "libbluray"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.5.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c3e85ef1-4134-3f56-b68e-98d1cb840d1e", "vendor": {"name": "VideoLAN"}}], "isExploited": false}